# Users — repository (DB connection layer)

The User aggregate is owned by this service. The persistence boundary is the `UserRepository` port in [`src/domain/ports/user.repository.ts`](../../src/domain/ports/user.repository.ts); the production implementation is `PrismaUserRepository` at `src/infrastructure/persistence/user.repository.ts` (TBD — create alongside the first prod-wired feature). Standard port → repository → Prisma chain. **No HTTP adapter, no mock-vs-real driver split, no `UsersModule` shell.**

## Port shape

| Method | Returns | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `findById(userId)` | `UserProfile \| null` | Caller decides whether `null` means 404. `UsersService` adds the not-found check. |
| `findByEmail(email)` | `UserProfile \| null` | Same pattern. Email is normalized (trim + lowercase) by the adapter. |
| `create(input)` | `UserProfile` | DB assigns `id` via `@default(uuid())`. Throws `UserAlreadyExistsError` on duplicate email. |
| `list(query)` | `UserProfilePage` | Atomic page+total via `prisma.$transaction([findMany, count])`. |
| `update(userId, input)` | `UserProfile` | Throws `UserNotFoundError` if missing. |
| `delete(userId)` | `void` | Throws `UserNotFoundError` if missing. |

DI token: `USER_REPOSITORY` (Symbol). Inject via `@Inject(USER_REPOSITORY)`.

## What `PrismaUserRepository` must do

- Implement every method on `UserRepository`.
- Omit `id` from `prisma.user.create({ data })` — the DB assigns the UUID.
- Map Prisma errors to domain errors at the boundary:
  - `P2002` (unique violation on `email`) → `UserAlreadyExistsError`
  - `P2025` (record not found on update/delete) → `UserNotFoundError`
- Map Prisma rows to domain entities via [`mappers/user.mapper.ts`](../../src/infrastructure/persistence/mappers/user.mapper.ts).
- Take `PrismaService` as its only constructor dependency. Never instantiate `PrismaClient`.

## Test fakes vs production repository

| Layer | What it uses | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Application unit tests | [`FakeUserRepository`](../../test/fakes/fake-user.repository.ts) (in-memory) | Fastest feedback. Mirrors the production contract. |
| HTTP e2e | `FakeUserRepository` overriding `USER_REPOSITORY` | Exercises controller + validation pipe + filter without Postgres. See [`test/users.e2e-spec.ts`](../../test/users.e2e-spec.ts). |
| Repository integration tests (TBD) | Real Postgres from compose, gated on `DATABASE_URL` | Verifies Prisma error → domain error mapping. Live as `*.integration-spec.ts` next to the source. |

Don't add branches or flags to the production repository to support tests. If a test needs different behavior, override the port with a hand-written fake at the DI boundary — that is the whole point of the port.

## Fixture data

Dev User / Customer / Vehicle rows are seeded by [`prisma/seed.ts`](../../prisma/seed.ts) — idempotent upserts on stable UUIDs. Apply via `npx prisma db seed`. E2E suites that need them run that after `migrate reset`. Tests that don't reference seeded data prefer the fake-repository pattern and skip the DB entirely.

Seed-file rules:
- Stable UUIDs. Pick once, never change — tests will hard-reference them.
- Deterministic: no `Date.now()`, no `Math.random()`. Fixed ISO strings for any timestamps.
- Minimal but realistic: enough rows to cover the scenarios in [`../../docs/scenario/content.md`](../../../docs/scenario/content.md) (Alice + Honda Civic at minimum).
- No PII. Names like `Alice Test`, emails like `alice@example.test`.

## Don'ts

- Don't add a `Mock*Repository` or `Http*Repository`. One Prisma repository per aggregate; tests use the in-memory fake.
- Don't put the repository under `src/modules/users/infrastructure/`. There is no `src/modules/` tree — repositories live in `src/infrastructure/persistence/`.
- Don't grow business logic in the fake. If branches show up, the test belongs at a different layer.
- Don't expose seed data from a controller. Fixtures are an internal concern.
- Don't `console.log` from the repository. Use the injected pino logger; trace correlation depends on it.
